<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ r.name }} · paper-trends</title>
<meta name="description" content="How {{ r.name }} changed {{ r.year_range[0] }}–{{ r.year_range[1] }}: rising and fading topics, new vocabulary, who publishes. Built from OpenAlex.">
{% if inline_css %}<style>{{ inline_css }}</style>{% else %}<link rel="stylesheet" href="report.css">{% endif %}
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vega@5.30.0"></script>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vega-lite@5.21.0"></script>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/vega-embed@6.26.0"></script>
</head>
<body>
{% if nav %}<nav class="masthead"><div class="row">
  <a class="brand" href="{{ './' if app_links else 'index.html' }}"{{ ' target="_top"' if app_links else '' }}>paper-trends</a>
  <div class="venues">
  {% for group, items in nav %}
    <span class="group">{{ group }}</span>
    {% for slug, short in items %}<a href="{{ ('?conference=' ~ slug) if app_links else (slug ~ '.html') }}"{{ ' target="_top"' if app_links else '' }} class="{{ 'current' if slug == r.slug else '' }}">{{ short }}</a>{% endfor %}
  {% endfor %}
  </div>
</div></nav>{% endif %}

<main class="page{{ ' embedded' if embedded else '' }}">
<header class="title">
  <div class="kicker">Publication trends · {{ r.year_range[0] }}–{{ r.year_range[1] }}</div>
  <h1>{{ r.name }}</h1>
  <div class="meta">
    <span><b>{{ "{:,}".format(r.n_papers) }}</b> papers</span>
    <span><b>{{ r.years|length }}</b> editions</span>
    <span><b>{{ "%.0f"|format(r.abstract_coverage * 100) }}%</b> with abstracts</span>
    <span>data from OpenAlex, fetched {{ r.generated }}</span>
  </div>
</header>

<section id="glance">
  <h2>At a glance</h2>
  <ul class="glance">{% for s in r.glance %}<li>{{ s }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
  <figure style="max-width: 520px; margin-top: 28px">
    <figcaption><span class="headline">Papers per year</span><span class="sub">{{ r.growth_sentence[0]|upper }}{{ r.growth_sentence[1:] }}; abstract coverage {{ "%.0f"|format(r.abstract_coverage * 100) }}%{{ r.coverage_note }}.</span></figcaption>
    <div class="viz" id="fig-papers"></div>
  </figure>
</section>

<section id="rising">
  <h2>What is rising</h2>
  <p class="lede">Share of papers that are <em>about</em> the phrase: it is in the title, used more than once, or used beyond the opening of the abstract{{ " (titles only: OpenAlex lacks most abstracts for this venue)" if r.text_mode == "title" else "" }}. A paper that only names a phrase in its first sentence is not counted. Ranked by the gain between the first half of the period ({{ r.year_range[0] }}–{{ r.split_year - 1 }}) and the second ({{ r.split_year }}–{{ r.year_range[1] }}).</p>
  <div class="grid">
  {% for t in r.rising %}
    <figure>
      <p class="term">{{ t.term }}</p>
      <p class="move">{{ "%.1f"|format(t.early*100) }}% → <span class="up">{{ "%.1f"|format(t.late*100) }}%</span></p>
      <div class="viz" id="fig-rise-{{ loop.index }}"></div>
    </figure>
  {% endfor %}
  </div>
  <p class="source">OpenAlex · paper-trends</p>
</section>

<section id="fading">
  <h2>What is fading</h2>
  <p class="lede">The same measure for the phrases losing the most share. A fading phrase is often a technique that became standard and stopped being worth mentioning.</p>
  <div class="grid">
  {% for t in r.falling %}
    <figure class="fading">
      <p class="term">{{ t.term }}</p>
      <p class="move">{{ "%.1f"|format(t.early*100) }}% → <span class="down">{{ "%.1f"|format(t.late*100) }}%</span></p>
      <div class="viz" id="fig-fall-{{ loop.index }}"></div>
    </figure>
  {% endfor %}
  </div>
  <p class="source">OpenAlex · paper-trends</p>
</section>

<section id="vocabulary">
  <h2>New vocabulary</h2>
  <p class="lede">Phrases that were almost absent before {{ r.split_year }} and now appear in at least one paper in a hundred. ✚ marks the first year a phrase shows up.</p>
  <figure style="max-width: 760px">
    <div class="viz" id="fig-emerging"></div>
    <p class="source">OpenAlex · paper-trends</p>
  </figure>
</section>

<section id="topics">
  <h2>How the field's topics shifted</h2>
  <p class="lede">{{ r.topic_sentence }}</p>
  <figure class="wide">
    <figcaption><span class="headline">Share of papers by dominant topic</span><span class="sub">Topics fitted with NMF on titles and abstracts; each paper assigned to its strongest topic. Smaller topics folded into “Other”.</span></figcaption>
    <div class="viz" id="fig-topics"></div>
    <p class="source">OpenAlex · paper-trends</p>
  </figure>
  <ul class="topic-list">
  {% for t in r.topics %}
    <li><span class="swatch" style="background: {{ topic_colors[loop.index0] if loop.index0 < topic_colors|length else other_color }}"></span><b>{{ t.label }}</b> — {{ t.terms[:6]|join(', ') }} <span style="color: var(--faint)">({{ t.papers }} papers)</span></li>
  {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="who">
  <h2>Who publishes</h2>
  <p class="lede">Papers with at least one author at the institution (a paper counts once per institution; subsidiaries and institutes are credited to their parent). The arrow is the change in share of papers between the two halves of the period.</p>
  <figure class="wide" style="margin-bottom: 36px">
    <figcaption><span class="headline">Where the papers come from</span><span class="sub">Share of papers with at least one author in the country, {{ r.year_range[0] }}–{{ r.year_range[1] }}. Countries without a paper are left blank.</span></figcaption>
    <div class="viz" id="fig-map"></div>
  </figure>
  <div class="two">
    <figure>
      <figcaption><span class="headline">Institutions</span></figcaption>
      <div class="viz" id="fig-inst"></div>
    </figure>
    <figure>
      <figcaption><span class="headline">Countries</span></figcaption>
      <div class="viz" id="fig-country"></div>
    </figure>
  </div>
  <p class="source">OpenAlex · paper-trends</p>
</section>

<footer class="about" id="about">
  <h2>About the data</h2>
  <p>Metadata for every {{ r.name }} paper from {{ r.year_range[0] }} to {{ r.year_range[1] }} was pulled from <a href="https://openalex.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenAlex</a> (CC0). Front matter such as title pages and session overviews is removed. Phrases are word sequences taken from titles and abstracts; OpenAlex has no full text. A paper counts for a phrase when it is about it — the phrase is in the title, repeated, or used beyond the opening of the abstract — so a sentence like “with the rise of artificial intelligence…” does not make a paper an AI paper. {% if r.n_common_hidden %}{{ r.n_common_hidden }} phrases that are common in three or more other fields ({{ r.common_examples|join(", ") }}…) are left out of the rankings, because they say little about this conference in particular. {% endif %}“Rising” and “fading” compare the pooled share of the first half of the period with the second.</p>
  <p>Topics come from non-negative matrix factorisation of TF-IDF vectors with a fixed seed, so they are reproducible; labels are the topic's top terms. Institution names and parent relationships are OpenAlex's, which are good but not perfect.</p>
  <details><summary>Coverage by year</summary>
    <table><thead><tr><th>Year</th><th class="num">Papers</th><th class="num">With abstract</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    {% for row in r.papers_per_year %}<tr><td>{{ row.year }}</td><td class="num">{{ row.papers }}</td><td class="num">{{ "%.0f"|format(row.abstracts / row.papers * 100) }}%</td></tr>{% endfor %}
    </tbody></table>
  </details>
  <p style="margin-top: 20px">Generated {{ r.generated }} by <a href="https://github.com/Minjia-Hu/paper-trends" target="_blank" rel="noopener">paper-trends</a>.</p>
</footer>
</main>

<script>
const specs = {{ specs_json }};
const opts = { actions: false, renderer: "svg" };
const jobs = Object.entries(specs).map(([id, spec]) => vegaEmbed("#" + id, spec, opts));
</script>
</body>
</html>
